# Orbit — auditor ship gate (locked)

Apply on **every** Orbit Short or long question before upload. Do not score or ship from stills alone. Video Auditor must watch the open VO.

## Intensity curve (Street Dog Salon → Orbit)

Source pattern: Street Dog Salon Video #1 — DECLARE → ASSESS → ISOLATE → PROCESS (valley) → BUILD → REVEAL (highest peak). Script energy like “Today we [verb] [number] [subject]”. **Orbit adapts the shape; do not copy their 60s / 6-phase clock onto Shorts.** Intensity must **finish higher than it started**.

### Shorts (22–27s only — never stretch to 60s)

1. **DECLARE (0–1s):** strange picture on screen + punch. Not Orbit. Concrete, like “not one sun” / “planets made of diamond”.
2. **ASSESS (next few seconds):** one hard fact or measurement. Not poetry.
3. **REVEAL (last 4s + loop):** return to the same picture. Thursday film title on screen. “watch the full film →”. The last beat is the **highest intensity**, not a fade.
4. **Do not** add a long PROCESS valley with 10–12 cuts. That is how we get ≥40s Shorts.

### Longs (18–25 min)

1. Same curve over the film: **declare** on the picture (first 3s) → **assess**/stakes by 15s → **isolate** a first peak → **process** valley is where Orbit **ACTS** (not hover) → **build** → **reveal** is the last 10s picture hold (highest image, Studio end screens). Never end on a baked subscribe card.
2. Intensity must finish higher than it started.

## Shorts diamond bar

Winner to beat: *We Found Planets Made of Diamond* (`M-VN84HCNls`, 223% viewed). Miss: black-hole fall (`B2STcIAF1lY`, 59 views, 53% viewed). Live Three Suns remake (`MDvAKtmKauw`) is the **8/10** pattern; old (`nAZRIBm5wJw`) was **4/10**.

1. **Open on the strange picture in 1s.** Not Orbit. Not a title card.
2. **Loop:** first ~3s and last ~4s are the same window. No mid-word seam.
3. **Captions** the whole Short. No holes.
4. **Thursday film title** on screen (~9–14s).
5. **Length 22–27s.** Never ship or schedule ≥40s.
6. **End CTA on screen:** “watch the full film →”. Description: film title + parent long URL only. Zero `/go/`.
7. **Concrete title.** Soft/abstract titles lose.
8. **Studio Related / watch next** → parent long.
9. **Recut = new YouTube id.** Leave old live until remake is public, then unpublish. Do not delete.

## Longs

Reference: Europa v02 · Last Star v11 · BH v09 · AW v05 · Fermi v20.

1. **First 3s = strange picture only.** No Orbit, no logo, no title, no “ORBIT / Stories from the sky”.
2. **Orbit after ~8s**, in the scene, not a sticker.
3. **Leftover brand sting:** cover picture only (hold last clean frame over the sting). Audio stays uncut so the sentence finishes. Hard-cutting the sting failed BH v08 (VO chopped “Today, Or…”).
4. **After the cover,** the original next shot (chapter card, camera turn) is fine.
5. **End:** 10s last real picture. Official YouTube Studio end screens (Subscribe + next film when an id exists). No baked like/subscribe graphic or VO.
6. **Recut = new id.** Do not mint until Video Auditor passes after watching the open VO, not stills. Leave old live until new is public, then unpublish.
7. **No `/go/`** unless this cut names the product in VO and on screen. Shorts stay zero affiliate. JWST v04 stays film-only (no `/go/jwst-book`).

## Do not

- Reuse a YouTube id to swap a file.
- Score or ship from stills alone.
- Batch-dump Shorts.
- Stretch Shorts to ~60s to fit Street Dog’s six phases — Orbit Shorts stay 22–27s (DECLARE → ASSESS → REVEAL only).
- Restore the old brand sting or baked subscribe outro. Older playbook lines that say “reuse brand sting + like/subscribe outro” are wrong.
